item.description:
Three people of the same company and branch:
• email / password — an employee with Credentials Vault → View (owns and bins the test items);
• branchEmail / branchPassword — the Branch Admin (branch user) of that employee's branch — the only one who restores or deletes Critical Vault items in the bin;
• adminEmail / adminPassword — a Vault Admin (client admin) — changes the Normal Vault retention period.

GET /recycle-bin?vault=normal|critical&tab=all|mine|team|soon&q=&page=&per_page=

The four tabs — All Items · Deleted by Me · Team Credentials · Expiring Soon — each with a Normal Vault and a Critical Vault sub-tab. vault (default normal) is the sub-tab.

Response:
• tabs — the chosen vault's four counts;
• counts — { normal: {all, mine, team, soon}, critical: {…}, total: {…} } — every badge at once; they follow the search box;
• summary — the cards of the chosen vault: retention_days, retention_fixed (Critical: true), can_change_retention (Normal + Vault Admin only), retention_options, items, deleted_by_me, expiring_soon (within 7 days of deletion), critical, next_deletion {name, at, days}, can_empty;
• data[] — sr_no, code, vault, name, type_label, category_group, url, scope / scope_label, risk, owner {name, initials}, deleted_by {name ('You'), initials}, deleted_at, purges_at, days_left, left_pct, urgency (ok · warn · bad), can_restore, can_purge, locked_reason;
• purged — items removed because their period ended.
